// src/v4/std/node.dag
//
// Scope: foundational substrate — type connectives + L1 behaviors. THE root of the epistemic chain.
// Anchor: THESIS.md "Substrate shape" §198-203 + MODELING.md
//
// Owns:
//   - 6 type connectives: Atom | Conj | Disj | Arrow | Cardinality | Instantiation
//   - 5 L1 behaviors: Value | Transform | Branch | Loop | Bind
//   - C1 stop-signal discipline (no 7th connective, no 6th behavior)
//   - Symbol: opaque kernel identity (K-1, operator-ratified 2026-05-15)
//   - Hash: opaque content-address digest (B1, operator-ratified
//     2026-05-15; re-homed from the deleted std/primitive.dag)
//   - Node / NodeKind / Edge: the one recursive type + its skeleton
//   - the edge-discipline structural invariant (a connective fixes its
//     edge shape; the illegal pairing is never silently constructible)
//   - D1 Diff family, DATA ONLY: Path / Edit / Diff — the
//     structural-delta vocabulary over Node (operator-ratified
//     2026-05-15; shape refined per a P2 review finding, PR #3162 —
//     see the D1 block below). The operations (subterm_at /
//     apply_diff) live in lens/application.dag, not here (forced
//     split — see the D1 block).
//
// A1 (operator-ratified 2026-05-15) — the recursion contract:
//   - ONE recursive type: Node. Recursion lives SOLELY in Node children
//     (the children list), never in a self-referential type definition.
//   - A Node carries ORTHOGONAL flat-discriminant coordinates — connective
//     (∈ the closed 6, incl. `Instantiation` which is how genericity is
//     expressed: parameter-names + the Instantiation connective, NOT a
//     recursive Generic type) and, for computation Nodes, behavior (∈ the
//     closed 5). The two-coordinated-substrate framing (THESIS §198-203)
//     = these axes stay orthogonal; it does NOT license a 2nd recursive
//     type. Behaviors are STRUCTURAL, never lens-derived (same discipline
//     as feedback_no_annotations); THESIS's uncommitted "unified substrate"
//     means *deriving behaviors away* — rejected here.
//   - A separate recursive Behavior / Inferred / Pattern / Generic type is
//     the bounded-kernel violation that split v2 infer into 12 files —
//     STOP and escalate, NOT a worker choice.
//   - Recursive generics: a recursive generic is a FINITE Node tree with
//     an `Instantiation` connective + a name-reference Node back to its
//     own declaration (resolved through the namespace — feedback_naming_is
//     _aliasing); it is "just Node underlying." Regular recursion (same
//     parameter at the recursive occurrence) is unconditionally admissible
//     and decidable. Non-regular / polymorphic recursion (recursive
//     occurrence at a different instantiation) is a STOP unless a decidable
//     bound is exhibited (defers to the A2 decidability resolution).
//
// A2 (operator-ratified 2026-05-15) — termination is Tier-1, not optional:
//   - `Loop` is BOUNDED RECURSION, total-by-construction (the
//     Coq/Agda/Idris totality choice — INVARIANTS:72). No Y-combinator,
//     no general recursion. This is the established INVARIANT P4 made
//     explicit as the T-1 substrate shape.
//   - Termination is a Tier-1 (compile-time) structural fact carried as
//     descent evidence: IMPLICIT when recursion descends on a sub-Node
//     (the bounded-kernel "recursion in children" default — the common
//     case, no measure needed); EXPLICIT RankingDimension/TerminationProof
//     (lexicographic/multiset per Dershowitz-Manna) when descent is not
//     structural.
//   - A CHECKER reading VERIFIES the descent proof (decidable). It never
//     searches/discovers a measure (INVARIANTS:66 "checker not discoverer"
//     = feedback_no_engine). `DescentUnknown` ⇒ fail-closed Diagnostic,
//     never a fabricated or assumed termination.
//   - The bound IS the structural datum lens/cost.dag reads — termination
//     ∧ complexity are ONE read on the U1 homomorphism-with-cost spine
//     (this is why C2 cost derivation is sound).
//   - Genuine unboundedness (servers/streams/REPLs) is a TERMINATING step
//     iterated by the coordination-boundary driver — never an unbounded
//     `.dag` loop.
//   - Residual boundary (ratified, not buried): a true-but-not-
//     structurally-rankable termination (open conjecture / un-encodable
//     math) is NOT expressible as a total value — express it as bounded
//     search returning a fail-closed typed result; you may not CLAIM a
//     totality you cannot prove. Where even that is impossible ⇒ STOP-
//     escalate (a modeling conversation, not a worker hack). Correct
//     closure of a decidable system (INVARIANTS:31), not a defect.
//
// K-1 (operator-ratified 2026-05-15) — kernel identifiers are opaque:
//   - `Symbol` is an opaque identity: equality-comparable and NOTHING
//     else. The type exposes no content accessor — kernel and lens code
//     physically cannot read or branch on an identifier's spelling.
//   - This forecloses the v2 failure mode structurally, not by review:
//     a readable kernel String became a heuristic-smuggling channel
//     (`match name { "x" => ... }`, prefix checks; INVARIANTS:229,
//     feedback_opaque_strings_attract_heuristics). With an opaque Symbol
//     the heuristic is UNWRITABLE — the type won't yield content
//     (feedback_no_textual_enforcement_bridges: structure, not a test).
//   - The human-readable spelling lives in a boundary intern table,
//     consulted ONLY at diagnostics rendering and emission — never by
//     kernel/lens logic. Whether Symbol is backed by a hash or an intern
//     index is hidden by the type (seed/runtime implementation detail).
//   - Bonus consistency: with opaque Symbol the content-hash fold over an
//     `Atom` is automatically rename-invariant — α-equivalent programs
//     hash equal — because the fold cannot observe the spelling.
//
// D1 (operator-ratified 2026-05-15; shape refined 2026-05-15 per a P2
// review finding on PR #3162 — codex REQUEST_CHANGES; the refinement is
// for operator confirm) — the structural-delta vocabulary:
//   - An `Edit` replaces the subtree at a `Path` with a replacement
//     `Node` (the term-rewriting `t[s]p`; the anchor term for a Path is
//     a *position* / *occurrence*, the practitioner form a JSON Pointer,
//     RFC 6901 — here restricted to member-name tokens, see below). The
//     TYPE is named `Path` (the route), not `Position` (operator pick:
//     a position is a coordinate, a path is how you get there).
//   - A `Path` is `List<Symbol>`: each step descends the `Named` edge
//     keyed by that opaque `Symbol`. Flat & finite — NOT a new
//     recursive type (A1: `Node` stays the SOLE recursion). Resolution
//     needs only `Symbol` EQUALITY (K-1 grants exactly that; no
//     spelling read) — K-1-clean, NOT K-1-exempt.
//   - NO positional / ordinal selector (P2 finding 1). An `Int` ordinal
//     admits negative / out-of-range values — EXACTLY the
//     representable-illegal-state this file DESIGNED OUT at the
//     `EdgeLabel`/`EdgeDiscipline` block (the `Positional` variant
//     carries no index — see `type EdgeLabel`, ~284, and its
//     "deliberately NO stored index" rationale, ~278). It is NOT
//     reintroduced. Positional-connective children
//     (Arrow/Cardinality/Instantiation) are therefore NOT individually
//     addressed: an Edit replaces the nearest enclosing `Named` subtree
//     (coarser granularity = the safe over-fire #3157 point 3 blesses).
//     Surgical positional addressing is a future operator-ratified
//     substrate extension, deliberately omitted — it would need an
//     ordinal primitive the consumes-nothing root cannot have (no
//     kernel `Nat`; a recursive Peano nat = A1 STOP). The omission is
//     structural honesty, not a deferral: the capability is reachable
//     today via enclosing-subtree replacement; any future surgical
//     need is an explicit ratification, never a silent TODO.
//   - NO well-formedness predicate (P2 finding 2). A `Diff` is an
//     ORDERED `List<Edit>` applied as SEQUENTIAL rewrites
//     (`root |> apply(e1) |> apply(e2) |> …`). There is NO "set /
//     pairwise-independent / parallel-positions" invariant: ANY
//     `List<Edit>` is a valid rewrite program, so no illegal state is
//     representable and there is nothing for an external predicate to
//     recover (the prior set+`diff_well_formed` shape was exactly the
//     illegal-states-representable anti-pattern the rubric blocks). An
//     Edit whose Path no longer resolves after earlier Edits ⇒ a
//     fail-closed Diagnostic at apply time (legitimate operational
//     behavior, NOT a type-level illegal state). `apply_diff` is a
//     fold; all-or-nothing — any failing step makes the whole result
//     that one Diagnostic.
//   - DATA-ONLY here. The operations — `subterm_at`/`apply_diff`
//     (`-> Result<Node, Diagnostic>`) — live in `lens/application.dag`,
//     NOT here. FORCED, not stylistic: `std/diagnostic.dag` already
//     `Consumes std/node.dag` (`Correction = Suggested(Node)`), so a
//     node.dag operation returning `Result<_, Diagnostic>` would make
//     node.dag depend back on Diagnostic = a substrate cycle. This is
//     exactly the discipline already stated for `node_well_formed`
//     below: the substrate root declares the structural data; CONSUMERS
//     evaluate fail-closed and raise the Diagnostic.
//   - Single authority for the Diff TYPES is here, by the B1/`Hash`
//     precedent: a structural delta over `Node` is substrate-tier, not
//     a lens's private type. Consumed by `lens/affected_set.dag` (T-21
//     `(Dag, Diff)` parameter), `lens/application.dag` (T-23
//     `apply_diff`), incremental eval, and structural caching.
//
// T-1 scope dispositions (operator-ratified 2026-05-15):
//   - Q1: `Atom` carries an opaque `Symbol` identity only. Literal VALUE
//     typing (int/string/bool literal data) is owned by the scalar/numeric
//     files — std/integer.dag, std/text.dag, std/logic.dag (T-3) — a
//     different concern from identifier identity.
//   - Q2: this file owns the `Loop` behavior variant + the A2 discipline
//     above; the descent-evidence carriers (RankingDimension /
//     TerminationProof / DescentEvidence) belong to std/cardinality.dag
//     (T-3, P4 decidability). The IMPLICIT descent case (recursion on a
//     proper sub-Node child) needs no carrier — it is free from A1's
//     children structure; only explicit non-structural ranking needs one.
//   - `inhabits` is NOT a field of `Node`: A1 forbids non-`children`
//     Node-recursion, and inhabitance is a cross-declaration relation
//     expressed via name-reference `Atom`s (resolved through the
//     namespace) — each inhabiting concrete type declares its OWN
//     inhabitance in its own concept file (std/integer.dag,
//     std/logic.dag, …); std/algebra.dag (T-2) owns only the algebra
//     STRUCTURES that get inhabited, never the inhabitance instances
//     (P2). (T-1-closeout correction 2026-05-15: the prior
//     "declared/owned by std/algebra.dag (T-2)" wording predated the
//     operator-ratified structures-only scope.)
//
// Consumes:
//   nothing — this is the substrate root
//
// Status: T-1 modeled 2026-05-15 (cool-boar-275). The I/O contract in
// this header is immutable for downstream workers. Splitting this file
// requires explicit operator ratification (substrate extension = stop
// signal).


module v4.std.node


// ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
// Symbol — opaque kernel identity (K-1).
//
// Body-less by design: an opaque type yields no content. Equality is the
// only operation; there is deliberately no accessor that returns the
// spelling. Symbol is substrate-ambient (declared at the substrate root,
// like the kernel List/Int/Bool) — it is not "consumed" from another
// file. See header K-1 for the full rationale.
type Symbol


// ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
// Hash — opaque content-address digest (B1, operator-ratified 2026-05-15).
//
// Body-less and opaque, exactly like `Symbol` (the K-1 discipline):
// equality only, no content accessor. `Hash` is the content-addressing
// carrier — the result of `content_hash : Node -> Hash`, a Merkle
// catamorphism over the canonical-form clause. That fold and the
// canonical-form clause are the T-1 closeout (B1: "T-1 worker encodes
// the clause + fold per relay"); THIS is the carrier type they produce.
// One scheme — consumed by T-15 (fixed point) / T-20 (pinned binary) /
// T-21 (affected-set + structural caching) / the A3 reproduction check /
// C5 RoundTrips. (Re-homed here from the deleted std/primitive.dag —
// `Hash` is a content identity, not a scalar; see STRUCTURE.md
// §"Scalar/numeric concept decomposition".)
type Hash


// ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
// Connective — the closed type-substrate classifier. Exactly six.
//
// `Atom` is terminal at the user-input boundary: it carries an opaque
// `Symbol` identity (an identifier / type-parameter name) and decomposes
// no further. The other five connectives are pure structural
// discriminants whose entire content is their `children` edges.
//
// CLOSED (C1 stop-signal). A seventh connective is an edit to THIS
// declaration — a visible diff routed to operator ratification (per
// STRUCTURE.md A3: the substrate does not magically refuse it; the edit
// is loud and un-missable). There is no `Other` / open-ended variant.
//
// Coproduct dissolution (Practice 4 / modeling-discipline.md §4) —
// 🟢 GREEN (terminal). Ledger — five patterns attempted:
//   1. Fact placement — FAILS: every pipeline stage (parse/normalize/
//      infer/emit) dispatches on the connective; it is the shared
//      classifier, not a per-consumer scattered fact.
//   2. Variant-is-data — FAILS: the six are structurally distinct
//      (Atom carries a Symbol; Conj/Disj labeled; Arrow/Cardinality/
//      Instantiation positional) — no uniform label space to fold.
//   3. Algebraic form — N/A by construction: this IS the type-substrate
//      root (THESIS:202); the connectives do not trace to a richer
//      std/ algebra — they are the source other structure grounds in.
//   4. Dimensional — FAILS: a node carries EXACTLY ONE connective;
//      genuine alternatives, never simultaneous coordinates.
//   5. Parameterized family — FAILS: the six are structurally
//      heterogeneous (Atom carries a Symbol; Conj/Disj labeled;
//      Arrow/Cardinality/Instantiation positional, distinct arities/
//      semantics) — NOT one generic `F<X>` / projection over a source
//      set X (Practice 7). No enumeration-to-projection collapse exists.
// Terminal: the closed 6 type connectives; a 7th is the C1 stop-signal
// (a visible ratified edit to this declaration, STRUCTURE.md
// commitment #1). Irreducible substrate root.
type Connective
  = Atom { identity: Symbol }
  | Conj
  | Disj
  | Arrow
  | Cardinality
  | Instantiation


// ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
// Behavior — the closed computation-substrate classifier. Exactly five.
//
// Flat unit variants: a behavior carries no payload. All structure (a
// Loop's body, a Branch's paths, a Transform's operands) lives in the
// owning Node's `children`. This file owns the five-behavior ENUM and
// the A2 `Loop`-is-bounded discipline; per-behavior edge wiring is built
// by the pipeline-stage tasks (T-6+).
//
// CLOSED (C1 stop-signal). A sixth behavior is an edit to THIS
// declaration — a visible diff routed to operator ratification.
//
// Coproduct dissolution (Practice 4 / modeling-discipline.md §4) —
// 🟢 GREEN (terminal). Ledger — five patterns attempted:
//   1. Fact placement — FAILS: every computation-substrate consumer
//      dispatches on the behavior; shared classifier, not scattered.
//   2. Variant-is-data — FAILS: the five are distinct computation
//      kinds (the typed-total-λ fragment per INVARIANTS — Transform=
//      application, Bind=let, Branch=sums, Loop=bounded rec, Value);
//      no uniform label space.
//   3. Algebraic form — N/A by construction: this IS the computation-
//      substrate root (THESIS:202); no richer std/ source.
//   4. Dimensional — FAILS: a computation node carries EXACTLY ONE
//      behavior; alternatives, not coordinates.
//   5. Parameterized family — FAILS: the five are distinct computation
//      kinds (the typed-total-λ fragment — Transform=application,
//      Bind=let, Branch=sums, Loop=bounded rec, Value) — NOT one
//      generic `F<X>` / projection over a source set (Practice 7).
// Terminal: the closed 5 L1 behaviors; a 6th is the C1 stop-signal
// (STRUCTURE.md commitment #1). Irreducible substrate root.
type Behavior
  = Value
  | Transform
  | Branch
  | Loop
  | Bind


// ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
// NodeKind — which of the two coordinated substrates a Node lives in.
//
// Shape S (operator-confirmed 2026-05-15): a Node belongs to EXACTLY one
// substrate. A type node has a connective; a computation node has a
// behavior. It is NOT the case that one node carries both — that would
// conflate the two independent C1 closures. The connective and behavior
// enums stay orthogonal closed sets; `NodeKind` merely selects which
// one applies (THESIS:198-203 — computation references type by edge, it
// does not co-locate the two coordinates on one node).
//
// Coproduct dissolution (Practice 4 / modeling-discipline.md §4) —
// 🟢 GREEN (terminal). Ledger — five patterns attempted:
//   1. Fact placement — FAILS: every Node consumer branches on kind
//      to know which substrate it is in; shared, not scattered.
//   2. Variant-is-data — FAILS: TypeNode carries a Connective,
//      ComputationNode a Behavior — disjoint payloads, no uniform
//      label space.
//   3. Algebraic form — N/A by construction: the two-coordinated-
//      substrate split IS the substrate shape (THESIS:198-203); no
//      richer source.
//   4. Dimensional — FAILS: Shape S — a Node is in EXACTLY ONE
//      substrate, never both; alternatives, not coordinates (co-
//      locating both would conflate the two independent C1 closures).
//   5. Parameterized family — FAILS: TypeNode/ComputationNode carry
//      disjoint payloads (Connective vs Behavior) — not one generic
//      `F<X>` / projection over a source set (Practice 7); it is the
//      irreducible two-coordinated-substrate selector.
// Terminal: the binary type/computation substrate split; irreducible.
type NodeKind
  = TypeNode { connective: Connective }
  | ComputationNode { behavior: Behavior }


// ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
// EdgeLabel — how a child Node is addressed from its parent.
//
// `Named` (carrying an opaque `Symbol` per K-1 — never a readable string)
// for the labeled-children connectives (Conj/Disj). `Positional` is a
// bare marker for the positional-children connectives (Arrow/Cardinality/
// Instantiation): a positional child's identity IS its 0-based position
// in the parent's `children` list. That list order is the SINGLE
// authority for positional order (CULTURE §8 — canonical, deterministic).
//
// There is deliberately NO stored index. A `Positional { index: Int }`
// field would duplicate the list order — a second authority that can
// disagree (INVARIANTS P2), and it is exactly that duplication that made
// negative / gapped / duplicate / out-of-order indices representable.
// With no index field those illegal states are STRUCTURALLY
// UNREPRESENTABLE — not "rejected by a checker."
//
// Coproduct dissolution (Practice 4 / modeling-discipline.md §4) —
// 🟢 GREEN (terminal). Ledger — five patterns attempted:
//   1. Fact placement — FAILS: every edge consumer branches on the
//      label kind uniformly; shared, not scattered.
//   2. Variant-is-data — FAILS: `Named` carries a Symbol; `Positional`
//      is a bare marker whose identity IS list position. Folding to a
//      uniform record means a stored index — the INVARIANTS P2
//      duplicate-authority anti-pattern this type exists to forbid.
//   3. Algebraic form — N/A by construction: the two child-addressing
//      modes are the edge-discipline primitive; no richer std/ source.
//   4. Dimensional — FAILS: an edge is EITHER named OR positional,
//      never both; alternatives, not coordinates.
//   5. Parameterized family — FAILS: `Named` carries a Symbol,
//      `Positional` is a bare marker (identity = list position) —
//      heterogeneous, NOT one generic `F<X>` / projection over a
//      source set (Practice 7).
// Terminal: the two child-addressing modes; the no-stored-index design
// makes illegal index states unrepresentable — this IS already the
// dissolved form, not a compression of one.
type EdgeLabel
  = Named { name: Symbol }
  | Positional


// Edge — a parent Node's reference to one child Node.
type Edge {
  label: EdgeLabel
  target: Node
}


// ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
// Node — THE one recursive type (A1).
//
// Recursion lives SOLELY in `children`: each Edge's `target` is a Node,
// reached only via the children list. There is no other self-reference —
// no `inhabits: Node` slot, no parent pointer. Cross-declaration
// references are name-reference `Atom`s resolved through the namespace
// (A1), which keeps every Node tree finite and the content-hash fold
// well-defined.
type Node {
  kind: NodeKind
  children: List<Edge>
}


// ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
// Edge-discipline invariant (operator directive D3, 2026-05-15).
//
// A connective FIXES its edge discipline: Conj/Disj address children by
// name (`Named`), Arrow/Cardinality/Instantiation by position
// (`Positional`), `Atom` is terminal with no children. The one illegal
// state left to guard is a label-KIND mismatch — a `Named` edge under a
// positional connective (or the reverse), or any edge under `Atom`.
//
// That mismatch is CHECK-enforced, not type-unrepresentable: making it
// unrepresentable would require connective-specific child collections —
// the per-connective redesign D3 explicitly declined ("keep one
// `children: List<Edge>` list"). `node_well_formed` is therefore the
// structural invariant consumers (parse / normalize) evaluate fail-closed
// (INVARIANTS P3).
//
// This is deliberately NOT justified by the STRUCTURE.md A3 precedent.
// A3 is checked-rather-than-unrepresentable because it guards an
// unpreventable human edit (Trusting-Trust — editing the seed). A
// malformed edge is an in-language VALUE — structurally preventable — so
// INVARIANTS P2 would prefer type-unrepresentability; the only reason it
// stays a check here is the D3 no-redesign call, not an A3-style
// impossibility. (Contrast: the closed `Connective` enum below — a 7th
// connective genuinely IS the A3 case, an edit to this file.)
//
// Coproduct dissolution (Practice 4 / modeling-discipline.md §4) —
// 🟢 GREEN (terminal). Ledger — five patterns attempted:
//   1. Fact placement — FAILS: derived uniformly from the connective
//      via `connective_edge_discipline` and consumed by
//      `node_well_formed`; single authority, not scattered.
//   2. Variant-is-data — FAILS: the three are distinct structural
//      rules (no edges / labeled+distinct / positional), not a uniform
//      label space.
//   3. Algebraic form — N/A by construction: it is the projection of
//      the closed `Connective` set's edge rule; it IS the rule, no
//      richer source.
//   4. Dimensional — FAILS: a connective fixes EXACTLY ONE discipline;
//      alternatives, not coordinates.
//   5. Parameterized family — FAILS: the three are distinct structural
//      rules (no edges / labeled+distinct / positional) — NOT one
//      generic `F<X>` / projection over a source set (Practice 7);
//      it is the irreducible projection OF the closed `Connective` set
//      onto its edge rule, already in dissolved form.
// Terminal: the three connective edge-disciplines; a closed classifier
// over the closed `Connective` set — irreducible with it.
type EdgeDiscipline
  = NoEdges
  | LabeledEdges
  | PositionalEdges


// The discipline a connective fixes for its children.
fn connective_edge_discipline(c: Connective) -> EdgeDiscipline {
  match c {
    Atom { identity: _ } => NoEdges
    Conj => LabeledEdges
    Disj => LabeledEdges
    Arrow => PositionalEdges
    Cardinality => PositionalEdges
    Instantiation => PositionalEdges
  }
}


// Is one edge addressed by name (`Named`) rather than by position?
fn edge_is_named(e: Edge) -> Bool {
  match e.label {
    Named { name: _ } => true
    Positional => false
  }
}

// Is one edge a positional edge? (Its position is its index in the
// parent's `children` list — there is nothing else to check.)
fn edge_is_positional(e: Edge) -> Bool {
  match e.label {
    Named { name: _ } => false
    Positional => true
  }
}

fn all_edges_named(children: List<Edge>) -> Bool {
  fold(children, init: true, f: fn(acc, e) {
    acc && edge_is_named(e: e)
  })
}

fn all_edges_positional(children: List<Edge>) -> Bool {
  fold(children, init: true, f: fn(acc, e) {
    acc && edge_is_positional(e: e)
  })
}

// How many of `children` carry the Named key `name`?
// (`Symbol` equality is the one operation K-1 grants the opaque type.)
fn name_occurrences(name: Symbol, children: List<Edge>) -> Int {
  fold(children, init: 0, f: fn(acc, e) {
    match e.label {
      Named { name: n } => if n == name { acc + 1 } else { acc }
      Positional => acc
    }
  })
}

// Are all Named keys distinct? A `Named` edge is an ADDRESS — two
// children sharing a key make "address a child by name" ambiguous, so a
// labeled connective with a duplicate key is malformed. Checked here so
// downstream consumers can treat a well-formed Conj/Disj's names as keys
// without each re-verifying uniqueness (INVARIANTS P2 — one authority).
fn all_names_distinct(children: List<Edge>) -> Bool {
  fold(children, init: true, f: fn(acc, e) {
    match e.label {
      Named { name: n } => acc && (name_occurrences(name: n, children: children) == 1)
      Positional => acc
    }
  })
}


// Do all of a node's edges satisfy the connective's discipline?
//   NoEdges          → the children list must be empty
//   LabeledEdges     → every edge is addressed by name AND all names are
//                      distinct (a name is an address — no duplicates)
//   PositionalEdges  → every edge is positional (order = list order)
fn edges_conform(children: List<Edge>, d: EdgeDiscipline) -> Bool {
  match d {
    NoEdges => count(children) == 0
    LabeledEdges =>
      all_edges_named(children: children) && all_names_distinct(children: children)
    PositionalEdges => all_edges_positional(children: children)
  }
}


// The LOCAL edge discipline of a single node (its own `children` only).
// A type node's connective fixes the discipline; a computation node has
// no local edge constraint at this substrate-root layer (see below).
fn node_locally_well_formed(n: Node) -> Bool {
  match n.kind {
    TypeNode { connective: c } =>
      edges_conform(children: n.children, d: connective_edge_discipline(c: c))
    ComputationNode { behavior: _ } => true
  }
}

// node_well_formed — the checked structural invariant (D3), WHOLE-TREE.
//
// A node is well-formed iff its own local edge discipline holds AND every
// child subtree is well-formed. This is ONE self-recursive function (not
// a mutual pair) so the v2 seed's termination analyzer accepts it — it
// recurses through `children` exactly the way v2's own recursive Node
// walks do (e.g. `check_bare_containers` in `src/v2/03_normalize.dag`).
// Termination is the A2 implicit case: each `e.target` is a proper
// sub-Node, structurally smaller, so the descent is finite.
//
// One call to `node_well_formed(root)` means the ENTIRE Node tree is
// well-formed — consumers (parse / normalize) do not traverse and
// re-check; that is the single-authority promise (INVARIANTS P2/P3).
//
// NAMED OBLIGATION ON T-6+ (not optional): the computation-node arm of
// `node_locally_well_formed` is an explicitly EMPTY local constraint —
// NOT "computation nodes are unconstrained, forever". The pipeline-stage
// tasks that build the computation substrate (T-6 tokenize … T-22 eval)
// MUST extend that arm with each behavior's edge discipline as they
// land. The whole-tree recursion here is already in force regardless.
fn node_well_formed(n: Node) -> Bool {
  node_locally_well_formed(n: n)
    && fold(n.children, init: true, f: fn(acc, e) {
         acc && node_well_formed(n: e.target)
       })
}


// ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
// D1 — the structural-delta vocabulary over Node (operator-ratified
// 2026-05-15; shape refined per a P2 review finding, PR #3162). DATA
// ONLY. The operations (subterm_at / apply_diff) live in
// lens/application.dag, NOT here — see the D1 header block above for
// the forced-by-cycle rationale (std/diagnostic.dag already depends on
// std/node.dag).
//
// Coproduct dissolution (Practice 4 / INVARIANTS P1 / modeling-
// discipline.md §4) — classification: 🟢 GREEN (DISSOLVED-AWAY,
// terminal). A prior shape carried a Path step as a sum
// `EdgeSelector = ByName { name: Symbol } | ByPosition { index: Int }`.
// That sum is dissolved, not retained; this receipt is the required
// substrate-shape artifact for that decision (PR #3162 BLOCKING — a
// D1 sum needs the ledger or it is not landable). Ledger — the four
// patterns attempted against "must a positional/ordinal selector
// variant exist":
//   1. Fact placement — DISSOLVES it. The "address a positional child"
//      fact has no independent consumer: every D1 consumer (affected_set
//      frontier seed, apply_diff, incremental eval, structural caching)
//      acts on edits expressible at NAMED-declaration granularity. A
//      positional-connective child (Arrow/Cardinality/Instantiation
//      param/result) is never the REQUIRED unit of an edit — any change
//      to it is expressible by replacing its enclosing `Named`
//      declaration's subtree wholesale (the replacement is a full Node
//      the caller rebuilds). The fact factors entirely through the
//      `ByName` step.
//   2. Variant-is-data — N/A once (1) removes the second variant: a
//      one-variant sum IS its payload, so `Path = List<Symbol>` — no
//      sum, no coproduct; the receipt obligation discharges itself.
//   3. Algebraic form — N/A: a Path step is not an algebraic structure;
//      it is a `Named`-edge key (`Symbol`), already owned by this file.
//      No richer std/ source to ground in.
//   4. Dimensional — FAILS as a reason to KEEP a positional variant:
//      addressing is never "by-name AND by-position" simultaneously;
//      positional internals are reached THROUGH the enclosing `ByName`
//      step, so there is exactly one addressing coordinate, not two.
// Terminal: positional addressing is structurally SUBSUMED by
// enclosing-`Named`-subtree replacement — coarser granularity #3157
// point 3 ratifies as safe over-fire, not lossy. This is NOT a deferred
// gap: the capability is reachable today; any future surgical/minimal-
// diff positional addressing is an explicit operator-ratified substrate
// extension (it would need an ordinal primitive the consumes-nothing
// root cannot host — no kernel `Nat`; a recursive Peano = A1 STOP),
// never a silent TODO. (An `Int` ordinal was rejected outright: it
// admits negative / out-of-range values — the representable-illegal-
// state this file designed out at `EdgeLabel`.)


// Path — the route from a root Node to a descendant: the ordered list
// of `Named`-edge keys to follow. `List<Symbol>`, NOT a new recursive
// type (A1: `Node` stays the sole recursion). The empty `steps` list
// denotes the root itself. Each step descends the `Named` edge keyed
// by that opaque `Symbol` (resolution = `Symbol` equality, K-1-clean).
// No positional/ordinal step — see the Practice-4 dissolution receipt
// above. Anchor term: a term-rewriting *position* / *occurrence*; the
// practitioner form is a JSON Pointer (RFC 6901) restricted to
// member-name tokens.
type Path {
  steps: List<Symbol>
}


// Edit — replace the subtree at `at` with `replacement` (the
// term-rewriting `t[replacement]at`). A deletion is a `replacement`
// whose cardinality is empty (expressed through the `Cardinality`
// connective) — never an `Option::None` sentinel (M5 / fail-closed).
type Edit {
  at: Path
  replacement: Node
}


// Diff — an ORDERED list of Edits applied as SEQUENTIAL rewrites
// (`root |> apply(e1) |> apply(e2) |> …`). There is deliberately NO
// set / pairwise-independence / "parallel positions" invariant: ANY
// `List<Edit>` is a valid rewrite program, so no illegal state is
// representable and no external well-formedness predicate exists to
// recover one (P2 finding 2, PR #3162 — the prior "set, validity via
// `diff_well_formed`" shape was exactly the illegal-states-representable
// anti-pattern). An Edit whose Path no longer resolves after earlier
// Edits ⇒ a fail-closed Diagnostic at apply time (legitimate
// operational behavior, NOT a type-level illegal state). `apply_diff`
// (lens/application.dag) is a fold; all-or-nothing — any failing step
// makes the whole result that one Diagnostic.
type Diff {
  edits: List<Edit>
}
